PIN TODO – Current Focus And Next Actions
========================================

Context
-------
The normalization + EMI pipeline now generates wrappers for complex typedef’d pointers and links against a clean libtiff build. Fuzzing `TIFFReadDirectory` reaches the real code path but crashes immediately because the stubbed handle provider returns `NULL`. The focus shifts from framework plumbing to supplying concrete library state, tightening EMI reporting, and preparing the next benchmarks (libpng, curl, etc.).

Open Challenges & Proposed Solutions
------------------------------------

1. External Handle Provisioning  
   • Problem: Auto-generated weak stubs (`pin_acquire_handle_*`) return `NULL`, so library entry points that require initialized state crash before EMI checks.  
   • Plan:  
     - Implement real handle factories per benchmark (e.g., reuse `tiff_read_directory_harness.c` logic to open a TIFF, wire callbacks, return `TIFF*`).  
     - Expose stub override hooks in `pin_diff.sh` so benchmarks can drop a `handle_glue.c` into the build.  
     - Document the pattern once for libtiff; replicate for OpenSSL/cURL session structs later.

2. EMI Diagnostics & Guard Telemetry  
   • Problem: Stage B summaries only show `emi-reject` vs `match`; we need richer stats (reason counts, first-occurrence samples) to compare against raw AFL baselines.  
   • Plan:  
     - Extend wrapper to accumulate per-reason counters (length mismatch, null slice, guard stub reject, etc.).  
     - Emit aggregated metrics at shutdown or via a JSON sidecar so fuzzing dashboards can read them.  
     - Update Stage B replay to ingest and print those counters alongside replay summaries.

3. Pointer Metadata Generalization  
   • Achieved: typedef chasing + include injection works without hand-editing wrappers.  
   • Remaining work:  
     - Skip generating proto messages for external structs automatically (already suppressed) and ensure future benchmarks add alias hints where needed.  
     - Add sanity check that warns when a struct pointer is marked external but no override function is linked (helps avoid the `NULL` crash loop).

4. Benchmark Roadmap  
   • libtiff: finish handle provider + EMI metrics, then rerun libFuzzer to measure time-to-crash vs AFL baseline.  
   • libpng: identify function-level CVE reproducer (e.g., palette processing), confirm typedef coverage, and plan handle/state provisioning.  
   • curl/OpenSSL: catalogue API entry points and note which require network/socket scaffolding before normalization.

5. Tooling Enhancements  
   • Provide a helper script to set `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` and launch `fuzz_bytes`/`normalized_bin` so the workflow is turnkey.  
   • Add build-clean lib paths to repo docs (CLAUDE.md) so future runs point at the sanitized libraries instead of AFL-instrumented ones.

Immediate Next Steps
--------------------
1. Implement `pin_acquire_handle_tif()` (and related release logic if needed) using the existing harness to return an initialized `TIFF*`.  
2. Re-run `fuzz_bytes` for a short window, verify EMI guards trigger (instead of ASan crash), and log reject counts.  
3. Capture baseline metrics (exec/s, first-crash time, coverage) and document them in `roadmap/libtiff-integration.md`.  
4. Generalize the handle-provider pattern into a minimal README section for new benchmarks.
